{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-004", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton continues to rise amid bullish factors", "content": "ICE cotton futures hit fresh highs as weaker US crop conditions, Texas and Xinjiang heat and dryness, and rising crude oil supported prices.\nChina's State Reserve auction saw a 26th consecutive sell-out, taking cumulative sales to 208,545 tonnes.\nOpen interest rose for a 16th session; further gains depend on textile mills accepting higher cotton prices and building orders.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-continues-to-rise-amid-bullish-factors-312925-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-005", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India urges Bangladesh to lift ban on yarn imports through land ports", "content": "India has urged Bangladesh to lift restrictions on yarn imports through land ports. The request was made by Indian high commissioner to Bangladesh Dinesh Trivedi to Commerce Minister Khandakar Abdul Muktadir. \nTrivedi discussed reopening closed border haats and fully operationalising land ports. \nIndia can back Bangladesh’s RMG sector by supplying zippers, machinery and other inputs, Trivedi said. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-urges-bangladesh-to-lift-ban-on-yarn-imports-through-land-ports-312923-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-006", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "MMCF cost divergence could reshape Q4 fibre sourcing", "content": "Modal 1.4 denier fibre prices stayed largely stable in Asia in the week ending August 21, 2026; China held at CNY 23,302 per tonne and Pakistan rose 0.27 per cent to PKR 756 per kilogram.\nIndia diverged as Domestic Modal 30/1 yarn rose 1.11 per cent to ₹273 and 40/1 rose 1.01 per cent to ₹299, while Tencel yarn jumped over 6 per cent amid tighter lyocell supply.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/mmcf-cost-divergence-could-reshape-q4-fibre-sourcing-312922-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-007", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh eyes global capital with $2-bn Hong Kong fund", "content": "Bangladesh plans a $2 billion equity fund in Hong Kong to widen business financing beyond conventional bank loans. \nExport sectors including ready-made garments, textiles, home textiles, leather and footwear could gain a capital route for upgrades. \nThe government is also weighing dollar, panda and samurai bonds while pursuing customs, tax and capital-market reforms. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-eyes-global-capital-with-2-bn-hong-kong-fund-312915-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-008", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Invest Bangladesh begins operations as unified investor platform", "content": "Bangladesh has launched Invest Bangladesh, merging its investment, economic-zone and public-private partnership agencies under the Prime Minister's Office. \nFor textile, apparel and sourcing investors, it centralises facilitation, zones, approvals, incentives and other government services. \nIt will retain BanglaBiz, work on 14-day business licensing and issue a progress report within 180 days. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/invest-bangladesh-begins-operations-as-unified-investor-platform-312901-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
